\n\n \n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a67f9f6d-10fe-54f7-8639-0a10309a8fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{3}:=R_{3} + 4R_{2}$\n$and$\n$R_{2}:=5R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114692} {:answer/id #uuid "34719fa3-8f0f-539a-80e1-c7c359d98ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{3}:=R_{2} + R_{1}$\n$and$\n$R_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114693} {:answer/id #uuid "47ee7b61-d8e4-536d-b6f4-47a49ea5ea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{3}:=R_{3} + 4R_{1}$\n$and$\n$R_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{5}R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114694} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7c054b-7e1d-5876-9971-9a8cacfcc12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{3}:=R_{3} + 4R_{1}$\n$and$\n$R_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114695} {:answer/id #uuid "63d56299-143e-551a-9f24-06b3fcfa4bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{3}:=R_{1} + 4R_{2}$\n$and$\n$R_{2}:=5R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114696}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f77b7547-a950-54ac-b67d-47439c952489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114691}] :question/id #uuid "f87950e1-533a-514d-b2aa-489417271ea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-78749" :question/problem "The inverse of $Q$ is found using row operations. Which row operations belong in the two blanks?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 &