te down $C$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $C$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,I] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}3 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -\\frac{4}{3} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -\\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${C}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{C}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e68556-9dc1-5987-97d3-f76d4edc298c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{3}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$\n$\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n${R}_{3}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346270} {:answer/id #uuid "8e49c9b2-b63e-5364-8bce-cec3389bdd3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1}$\n$\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346588} {:answer/id #uuid "c95b41ae-0717-504c-b5d7-55a61815dfdb" :a